        "text": "Hi All,\n\nWe're two weeks out from <https:\/\/rseaa.org\/|Research Software Asia Australia (RSAA26)>, <https:\/\/www.research-software-africa.org\/|Research Software Africa (RSAfrica26)> and <https:\/\/rs-latam.org\/|Research Software Latinoamérica (RSLA26)> - and things are coming together nicely.\n\nThanks to our generous sponsors for making this possible. This includes our Asia Spotlight Partner <https:\/\/www.access-nri.org.au\/|ACCESS-NRI> for supporting us, as well as our Accessibility Partners,<https:\/\/society-rse.org\/| the Society of RSE>, <https:\/\/linux.org.au\/|Linux Australia>, and the <https:\/\/www.software.ac.uk\/|Software Sustainability Institute>. We would also like to thank our Trust and Identity Partner <https:\/\/aaf.edu.au\/|Australian Access Federation (AAF)>, and our Supporting Partner <https:\/\/ardc.edu.au\/|ARDC> for their contribution.\n\nIf you haven't already, <https:\/\/rseaa.org\/|registration is still open until the 19th of August - along with scholarship opportunities> for those who need support.\n\nThese scholarships are available people who are:\n• unemployed,\n• undergraduate students,\n• Masters or PhD students,\n• in precarious employment,\n• financially pressured,\n• lack conference presentation opportunities,\n• don’t have a credit card to purchase tickets,\n• have had a career transition or gap,\n• are underrepresented in their field,\n• have caring duties, or\n• feel uncomfortable asking supervisors for funding.\nIf you don’t fit neatly into these categories but face other barriers to attendance, we encourage you to apply as we’re here to support you.\nCheck out the <https:\/\/rseaa.org\/program|full program for RSAA26 >here to see what's coming up as well as the <https:\/\/www.research-software-africa.org\/program.html|full program for RSAfrica26>. We've got some great sessions lined up. The RSLA26 program is expected to come out soon.",
